 from  home which ended with the post-credits  scene that brought back jk simmons and j  jonah jameson a cross-universe cameo  that also doesn't make a whole lot of  logical sense when you think about it  but the fans still loved it nonetheless  and just assumed that jk simmons could  play the same character in different  universes and sony from that likely  assumed that we would all have the same  thrilled reaction to michael keaton  probably a mistake leaning on keaton so  heavily for the marketing giving fans a  false impression of what this movie  would be instead of leaving keaton as a  surprise for which our appreciation  would outshine our overthinking but at  any rate the pandemic shut everything  down in march 2020 and morbius got  delayed first to march 2021 then to  october 2021 then to january 2022 and  then finally to april 2022 and in the  midst of all this sony who is always  under pressure to release new spider-man  films about every two years to retain  their film rights to the character  shuffled up the schedule so that  spider-man no way home would come out in  december 2021 before morbius so espinoza  said that it was hard to see morbius a  movie shot from february 2019 and  wrapped by june 2019 meaning they  started shooting this before end game  came out it was hard for him to see this  movie mostly locked now coming out in a  world after superhero movie expectations  completely shifted so it sounds like  michael keaton was intended to be a  post-credits scene cameo who meets  morbius which is why in earlier trailers  the two crossed paths you and i should  stay in touch  but after the movie got delayed to its  final april 2022 release date a decision  that was made in early january after no  way home came out trailers that were  released after that downplayed tomb's  interaction with morbius and instead  showed new footage of him alone in his  prison cell suggesting that much of this  was completely reconfigured after no way  home came out and in an interview with  uproxx espinosa confirmed that the  release of spider-man no way home  totally changed how sony wanted tomb's  arrival to look like in the morbius film  he said when spider-man nomihum came out  sony said this is how the visual effects  are and then the idea of having him just  encountering him in that universe seemed  too complicated and then we put it in  the end we have to match i don't know  how the transportation would look like  in that there were all these small  things that had to be addressed but i  think that the concept of having  different timelines were i believe came  from sony not from kevin feige it was  sony that initiated that idea so in  other words espinoza wanted to just have  morbius casually encounter tombs similar  to how peter parker casually sees j.k  simmons as shiron jameson as someone  already existing in that universe but  then after no way home sony insisted  that this scene use the same purple sky  cracks and the same white glowing  teleporting as the multiverse crossovers  in no way home problem is by doing that  sony really anchored morbius to the no  way home multiverse logic despite  honestly none of us fully understanding  that movie's logic still fans walked out  of it in the weeks after that movie  inferring enough logic that we needed to  process the movie but clearly sony did  not understand their own movie's  implications and by trying to use that  complicated logic to explain something  that didn't need an explanation they  ultimately implied adrian toombs  permanently left the mcu and entered a  universe where he has no resources and  no relationship with spider-man making  it completely nonsensical that he would  have his same vulture wings once more  and have any feelings whatsoever towards  this universe's spider-man still there  is a silver lining folks and that is  that this universe that tombs has just  joined still has a chance to be a really  awesome universe the director confirmed  that the 